> Conclusion

Narrow squeeze layers reduce spatial-filter budgets; expand branches, ceil pooling and the
ReLU class-map head define the full released behavior. Exact value/gradient fixtures and visible
Adam loops make those choices and their small-data limitations reviewable.

> References

- [Iandola et al. (2016), SqueezeNet](https://arxiv.org/abs/1602.07360).
- [Authors' release](https://github.com/forresti/SqueezeNet).
- [CIFAR-10 dataset](https://www.cs.toronto.edu/~kriz/cifar.html).
